      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a client requests OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ | OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WRITE, the fds_num_write_opens counter is incremented to 1 (because write access is requested).\n\nThe first condition (args-\u003eshare_access \u0026 OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ \u0026\u0026 file_stats-\u003efds_num_write_opens \u003e 0) evaluates to true because both the read bit is set AND there\u0027s a write open (the current one) and triggers the contention check and denies the delegation.\n\nThe new check !(args-\u003eshare_access \u0026 OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WRITE) ensures that:\n- Read-only clients (OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ only): Still denied delegation when write clients exist.\n\n- Write-only clients (OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WRITE only): Still denied delegation when multiple write clients exist.\n\n- Read+write clients (OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ | OPEN4_SHARE_ACCESS_WRITE): Treated like write clients, not read clients, so they can receive delegations when appropriate.\n\nSuch requests having mixed-access are used in PYNFS delegation test cases. I have changed the comment.",
